<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 656" role="img" aria-labelledby="title desc">
<title id="title">Zane Wang — building tools that make AI coding agents more reliable</title>
<desc id="desc">A pixel-art sunset over a city drawn from the past year of Zane's GitHub contributions: one building per week, one window per day, lit on the {{ACTIVE_DAYS}} days he contributed, and a gold pennant over each week in which one of his pull requests was merged upstream. Below the city: 12 PRs merged into 10 upstream projects ({{MERGED_RANGE}}): axum, SQLx, AnyIO, goose, Fastify, Zod, TanStack Query, Tenacity, Feast and Claude HUD (three), 10 bug fixes and 2 small features, for example pre-1970 SQLite datetimes that SQLx decoded up to 2 seconds off, and AnyIO's CapacityLimiter over-granting tokens. His production background covers multimodal evaluation and data systems; his current public focus is tools for reliable AI coding agents: claudemem, handoff and dev-orchestrator.</desc>
<!-- Fonts: Departure Mono (c) Helena Zhang and IBM Plex Mono (c) IBM Corp., both SIL Open Font License 1.1; embedded as renamed subsets. -->
<!-- The phone layout of dusk.svg.template, served by the README's <picture> below 600 px: authored 320 units wide
     for a README column of about 300-350 px, on a 2-unit pixel grid. Plex Mono sizes give whole-unit
     advances (0.6 em), so lines measure the same on every platform. text-rendering:geometricPrecision keeps
     them exact when the image is scaled: Chrome otherwise rounds each advance to a whole screen pixel. Type: 11 pixel labels, 11.67 notes
     (7-unit advance), 13.33 tagline (8), 15 names (9), 22 figures, 44 name. -->
<defs><style>{{FONT_FACES}}
text{text-rendering:geometricPrecision}
.px{font-family:zw-pixel, ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace}
.bd{font-family:zw-body, ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace}
.md{font-family:zw-body-medium, ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace}
.b{transform-box:fill-box;transform-origin:50% 100%;animation:rise 1s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1) both}@keyframes rise{from{transform:scaleY(0)}to{transform:scaleY(1)}}
.w{animation:on .6s ease-out both}@keyframes on{from{opacity:0}to{opacity:1}}
.tw{animation:tw 3.4s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes tw{0%,100%{opacity:.2}50%{opacity:.95}}
.glow{animation:glow 7s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes glow{0%,100%{opacity:.75}50%{opacity:1}}
.sh{animation:sh 2.8s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes sh{0%,100%{opacity:.25}50%{opacity:.9}}
.beacon{animation:bk 1.6s steps(1) infinite}@keyframes bk{0%{opacity:1}50%{opacity:.15}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important}}</style>
